        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Gate rate limit.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">gateRateLimit</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPInformationMessage.localReference -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPInformationMessage.localReference">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPInformationMessage"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The Local Reference attribute specifies a value agreed upon between sender and receiver of the Information Message. It further identifies the Information Message.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">localReference</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.calling -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.calling">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Used to indicate if the Provider is responsible for initiating the TASE.2 connection.  If the value is TRUE the provider is responsible for establishing the association.  If the value is FALSE the peer provider of the Bilateral Table will need to establish the association.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">calling</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.clientAndServer -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.clientAndServer">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>If True the value indicates that the entity represented by the bilateral table is capable of issuing requests and responding to request e.g. bidirectional support of ICCP requests.If False this indicates that a calling entity e.g. calling  True will not be able to respond to ICCP requests.  If False and callingFalse this indicates that the entity will only respond to ICCP requests and not issue ICCP requests.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">clientAndServer</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.minimumUpdateInterval -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.minimumUpdateInterval">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifies the fastest update interval that can be provided for integrity information and Transfer Set creation. The value is in seconds.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">minimumUpdateInterval</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.nameOfLocalICC -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.nameOfLocalICC">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifies the ICC scope name that the remote can use to access the information in the Bilateral Table if the information is not VCC scoped.  This value may not be null.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">nameOfLocalICC</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock1 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock1">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Per IEC 608706702  If true indicates support for basic services.  Must always be true.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">supportForBlock1</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock2 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock2">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Per IEC 608706702  If true indicates support for extended conditions.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">supportForBlock2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock3 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock3">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Per IEC 608706702  If true indicates support for blocked transfers. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">supportForBlock3</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock4 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock4">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Per IEC 608706702  If true indicates support for information messages. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">supportForBlock4</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock5 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForBlock5">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Per IEC 608706702  If true indicates support for device control. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">supportForBlock5</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForDepriciatedBlock8 -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.supportForDepriciatedBlock8">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Per IEC 608706702  If true indicates support for accounts.  The use of this block was deprecated in Edition 3.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">supportForDepriciatedBlock8</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.transportSecurityRequirement -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre.transportSecurityRequirement">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ICCPVirtualControlCentre"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>If true then transport level security as specified by IEC 623516 is required.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">transportSecurityRequirement</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IPAccessPoint.address -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IPAccessPoint.address">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IPAccessPoint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Is the dotted decimal IP Address resolve the IP address. The format is controlled by the value of the addressType.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">address</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IPAccessPoint.gateway -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IPAccessPoint.gateway">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IPAccessPoint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Is the dotted decimal IPAddress of the first hop router.  Format is controlled by the addressType.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">gateway</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IPAccessPoint.subnet -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IPAccessPoint.subnet">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IPAccessPoint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>This is the IP subnet mask which controls the local vs nonlocal routing.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">subnet</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.aeInvoke -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.aeInvoke">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Is part of the Application Entity addressing as specified by ISO Addressing.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">aeInvoke</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.aeQual -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.aeQual">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Is the AE qualifier and represents further application level addressing information.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">aeQual</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.apInvoke -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.apInvoke">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Is a further application level OSI addressing parameter.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">apInvoke</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.apTitle -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.apTitle">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Is a sequence of integer strings separated by ..  The value in conjunction with other application addressing attributes e.g. other APs are used to select a specific application e.g. the ICCP application entity per the OSI reference model.  The sequence and its values represent a namespace whose values are governed by ISOIEC 74983.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">apTitle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.osiPsel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.osiPsel">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Is the addressing selector for OSI presentation addressing.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">osiPsel</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.osiSsel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.osiSsel">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Is the OSI session layer addressing information.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">osiSsel</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.osiTsel -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer.osiTsel">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ISOUpperLayer"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Is the OSI Transport Layer addressing information.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">osiTsel</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject.aliasName -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject.aliasName">
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/saref#hasName"/>
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The aliasName is free text human readable name of the object alternative to IdentifiedObject.name. It may be non unique and may not correlate to a naming hierarchy.The attribute aliasName is retained because of backwards compatibility between CIM relases. It is however recommended to replace aliasName with the Name class as aliasName is planned for retirement at a future time.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">aliasName</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#InUseDate.inUseDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#InUseDate.inUseDate">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#InUseDate"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Date asset was most recently put in use.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">inUseDate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#InUseDate.notReadyForUseDate -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#InUseDate.notReadyForUseDate">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#InUseDate"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Date of most recent asset transition to not ready for use state.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">notReadyForUseDate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


