        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>freeform list of the equipment to be isolated by the switching</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">equipmentToBeIsolated</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.groundingPoints -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.groundingPoints">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>freeform list of equipment to be grounded or other actions to be taken in order to accomplish the required grounding.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">groundingPoints</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.isolationArea -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.isolationArea">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>freeform description of the area to be isolated by the switching</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">isolationArea</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.isolationPoints -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.isolationPoints">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>freeform list of equipment to be operated or other actions to be taken in order to accomplish the required isolation. </rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">isolationPoints</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.purpose -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.purpose">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">purpose</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.switchingRequestDetails -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest.switchingRequestDetails">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingPlanRequest"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">switchingRequestDetails</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStep.isFreeSequence -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStep.isFreeSequence">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStep"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>For a step if isFreeSequence is set to false or is not specified all of the steps in the group must be executed in the order defined by the sequenceNumber attribute. The sequenceNumber for a step has a different meaning when there are two or more sequential steps that have the isFreeSequence attribute set to true. Execution must still be performed in sequenceNumber order until a set of two or more steps that have isFreeSequence set to true is encountered. In this case these steps can be executed in any sequence until a step is encountered that has isFreeSequence set to false. All of the steps preceding this step must be executed before the step can be executed.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">isFreeSequence</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStep.subStepSequenceNumber -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStep.subStepSequenceNumber">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStep"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Supports compound switching steps that are made up of several sub steps.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">subStepSequenceNumber</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStepGroup.isFreeSequence -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStepGroup.isFreeSequence">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStepGroup"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>If true the sequence number serves for presentation purposes only and the activity itself may be executed at any time.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">isFreeSequence</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStepGroup.purpose -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStepGroup.purpose">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SwitchingStepGroup"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Describes the overall purpose of the steps in this switching step group.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">purpose</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachine.coolantCondition -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachine.coolantCondition">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachine"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Temperature or pressure of coolant medium.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">coolantCondition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachine.earthing -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachine.earthing">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachine"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Indicates whether or not the generator is earthed. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">earthing</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachine.mu -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachine.mu">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachine"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Factor to calculate the breaking current Section 4.5.2.1 in IEC 609090.Used only for single fed short circuit on a generator Section 4.3.4.2. in IEC 609090.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">mu</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineDetailed.efdBaseRatio -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineDetailed.efdBaseRatio">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineDetailed"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Ratio exciter voltagegenerator voltage of iEfdi bases of exciter and generator models gt 0. Typical value  1.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">efdBaseRatio</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineDetailed.saturationFactor120QAxis -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineDetailed.saturationFactor120QAxis">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineDetailed"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Quadratureaxis saturation factor at 120 of rated terminal voltage iS12qi gt SynchonousMachineDetailed.saturationFactorQAxis.  Typical value  012.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">saturationFactor120QAxis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineDetailed.saturationFactorQAxis -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineDetailed.saturationFactorQAxis">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineDetailed"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Quadratureaxis saturation factor at rated terminal voltage iS1qi gt 0. Typical value  002.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">saturationFactorQAxis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineTimeConstantReactance.ks -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineTimeConstantReactance.ks">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SynchronousMachineTimeConstantReactance"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Saturation loading correction factor iKsi gt 0.  Used only by type J model.  Typical value  0.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ks</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SysLoadDistributionFactor.factor -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SysLoadDistributionFactor.factor">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SysLoadDistributionFactor"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Used to calculate load participation of a connectivity node in an host control area</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">factor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TASE2BilateralTable.bilateralTableID -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TASE2BilateralTable.bilateralTableID">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TASE2BilateralTable"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifies the version of the Bilateral Table configuration that is being exchanged.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">bilateralTableID</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TASE2BilateralTable.bilateralTableVersion -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TASE2BilateralTable.bilateralTableVersion">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TASE2BilateralTable"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The Version attribute identifies a unique version of the Bilateral Table. If any changes are made to a Bilateral Table then a new unique value for this attribute shall be generated.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">bilateralTableVersion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TASE2BilateralTable.tase2version -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TASE2BilateralTable.tase2version">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TASE2BilateralTable"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifies the version of the TASE.2 that is needed to access the Bilateral Table information via TASE.2.In order for a link to be established both sides must have the same value.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tase2version</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TCPAccessPoint.keepAliveTime -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TCPAccessPoint.keepAliveTime">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TCPAccessPoint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Indicates the default interval at which TCP will check if the TCP connection is still valid.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">keepAliveTime</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TCPAccessPoint.port -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TCPAccessPoint.port">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TCPAccessPoint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>This value is only needed to be specified for called nodes e.g. those that respond to a TCP.Open request.This value specifies the TCP port to be used. Well known and registered ports are preferred and can be found at httpwww.iana.orgassignmentsservicenamesportnumbersservicenamesportnumbers.xhtmlFor IEC 608706 TASE.2 e.g. ICCP and IEC 61850 the value used shall be 102 for nonTLS protected exchanges. The value shall be 3782 for TLS transported ICCP and 61850 exchanges.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">port</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.highStep -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.highStep">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Highest possible tap step position advance from neutral.The attribute shall be greater than lowStep.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">highStep</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.ltcFlag -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.ltcFlag">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifies whether or not a TapChanger has load tap changing capabilities.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ltcFlag</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.neutralStep -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.neutralStep">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The neutral tap step position for this winding.The attribute shall be equal to or greater than lowStep and equal or less than highStep.It is the step position where the voltage is neutralU when the other terminals of the transformer are at the ratedU.  If there are other tap changers on the transformer those taps are kept constant at their neutralStep.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">neutralStep</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.normalStep -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.normalStep">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The tap step position used in normal network operation for this winding. For a Fixed tap changer indicates the current physical tap setting.The attribute shall be equal to or greater than lowStep and equal to or less than highStep.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">normalStep</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.step -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger.step">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChanger"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Tap changer position.Starting step for a steady state solution. Non integer values are allowed to support continuous tap variables. The reasons for continuous value are to support study cases where no discrete tap changer has yet been designed a solution where a narrow voltage band forces the tap step to oscillate or to accommodate for a continuous solution as input.The attribute shall be equal to or greater than lowStep and equal to or less than highStep.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">step</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerControl.lineDropCompensation -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerControl.lineDropCompensation">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerControl"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>If true the line drop compensation is to be applied.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">lineDropCompensation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.angleRegulationStatus -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.angleRegulationStatus">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>True means the phase shifter is regulating.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">angleRegulationStatus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.desiredMW -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.desiredMW">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Phase Shifter Desired MW. The active power regulation setpoint of the phase shifter</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">desiredMW</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.desiredVoltage -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.desiredVoltage">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The desired voltage for the LTC</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">desiredVoltage</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.maximumAngle -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.maximumAngle">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The maximum phase angle shift of the phase shifter</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">maximumAngle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.minimumAngle -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.minimumAngle">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The minimum phase angle shift of the phase shifter</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">minimumAngle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.solvedAngle -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.solvedAngle">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Phase Shifter Angle. The solved phase angle shift of the phase shifter</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">solvedAngle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.tapPosition -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.tapPosition">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Tap position of the phase shifter highside tap position of the transformer or  lowside tap position of the transformer</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tapPosition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.voltageRegulationStatus -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData.voltageRegulationStatus">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerDynamicData"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Indicator if the LTC transformer is regulating True  Yes False  No</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">voltageRegulationStatus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.ctRatio -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.ctRatio">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Builtin current transducer ratio.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ctRatio</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.highStep -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.highStep">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Highest possible tap step position advance from neutral.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">highStep</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.isTcul -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.isTcul">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Whether this tap changer has under load tap changing capabilities.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">isTcul</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.neutralStep -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.neutralStep">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The neutral tap step position for the winding.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">neutralStep</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.ptRatio -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo.ptRatio">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerInfo"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Builtin voltage transducer ratio.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ptRatio</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerTablePoint.ratio -->

    <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerTablePoint.ratio">
        <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#TapChangerTablePoint"/>
        <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The voltage at the tap step divided by rated voltage of the transformer end having the tap changer. Hence this is a value close to one.For example if the ratio at step 1 is 1.01 and the rated voltage of the transformer end is 110kV then the voltage obtained by setting the tap changer to step 1 to is 111.1kV.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ratio</rdfs:label>
    </owl:DatatypeProperty>
    


