    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePointConnectedKind.connected -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePointConnectedKind.connected">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePointConnectedKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The usage point is connected to the network and able to receive or send the applicable commodity electricity gas water etc..</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">connected</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePointConnectedKind.logicallyDisconnected -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePointConnectedKind.logicallyDisconnected">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePointConnectedKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The usage point has been disconnected through operation of a disconnect function within the meter present at the usage point.  The usage point is unable to receive or send the applicable commodity electricity gas water etc.  A logical disconnect can often be achieved without utilising a field crew.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">logicallyDisconnected</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePointConnectedKind.physicallyDisconnected -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePointConnectedKind.physicallyDisconnected">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePointConnectedKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The usage point has been disconnected from the network at a point upstream of the meter. The usage point is unable to receive or send the applicable commodity electricity gas water etc.. A physical disconnect is often achieved by utilising a field crew.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">physicallyDisconnected</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Validity.GOOD -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Validity.GOOD">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Validity"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The value is marked good if no abnormal condition of the acquisition function or the information source is detected.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">GOOD</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Validity.INVALID -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Validity.INVALID">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Validity"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The value is marked invalid when a supervision function recognises abnormal conditions of the acquisition function or the information source missing or nonoperating updating devices. The value is not defined under this condition. The mark invalid is used to indicate to the client that the value may be incorrect and shall not be used.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">INVALID</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Validity.QUESTIONABLE -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Validity.QUESTIONABLE">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Validity"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The value is marked questionable if a supervision function detects an abnormal behaviour however the value could still be valid. The client is responsible for determining whether or not values marked questionable should be used.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">QUESTIONABLE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind.contractor -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind.contractor">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Contractor vehicle.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">contractor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind.crew -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind.crew">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Crew vehicle.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">crew</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind.other -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind.other">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Other vehicle.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">other</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind.user -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind.user">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VehicleUsageKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>User vehicle.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">user</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.pPcc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.pPcc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Control is real power at point of common coupling. The target value is provided by ACDCConverter.targetPpcc.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pPcc</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.pPccAndUdcDroop -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.pPccAndUdcDroop">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Control is active power at point of common coupling and local DC voltage with the droop. Target values are provided by ACDCConverter.targetPpcc ACDCConverter.targetUdc and VsConverter.droop.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pPccAndUdcDroop</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.pPccAndUdcDroopPilot -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.pPccAndUdcDroopPilot">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Control is active power at point of common coupling and the pilot DC voltage with the droop. The mode is used for Multi Terminal High Voltage DC MTDC systems where multiple HVDC Substations are connected to the HVDC transmission lines. The pilot voltage is then used to coordinate the control the DC voltage across the HVDC substations. Targets are provided by ACDCConverter.targetPpcc ACDCConverter.targetUdc and  VsConverter.droop.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pPccAndUdcDroopPilot</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.pPccAndUdcDroopWithCompensation -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.pPccAndUdcDroopWithCompensation">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Control is active power at point of common coupling and compensated DC voltage with the droop. Compensation factor is the resistance as an approximation of the DC voltage of a common real or virtual node in the DC network. Targets are provided by ACDCConverter.targetPpcc ACDCConverter.targetUdc VsConverter.droop and VsConverter.droopCompensation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pPccAndUdcDroopWithCompensation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.phasePcc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.phasePcc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Control is phase at point of common coupling. Target is provided by VsConverter.targetPhasePcc.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">phasePcc</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.udc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind.udc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsPpccControlKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Control is DC voltage  with target value provided by ACDCConverter.targetUdc.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">udc</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind.powerFactorPcc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind.powerFactorPcc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Control is power factor at point of common coupling. Target is provided by VsConverter.targetPowerFactorPcc.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">powerFactorPcc</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind.pulseWidthModulation -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind.pulseWidthModulation">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>No explicit control. Pulsemodulation factor is directly set in magnitude VsConverter.targetPWMfactor and phase VsConverter.targetPhasePcc.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pulseWidthModulation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind.reactivePcc -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind.reactivePcc">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Control is reactive power at point of common coupling. Target is provided by VsConverter.targetQpcc.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">reactivePcc</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#VsQpccControlKind.voltagePcc -->

